# Edge redirects for Cloudflare Workers Assets (processed by the asset layer,
# before the Worker, exactly like the sibling _headers file).
#
# PERMANENTLY route the old app's entry routes to the rebuilt v2 SPA, so old
# bookmarks, deep links and installed-PWA launches (manifest start_url "/") land on
# v2. The old entry pages and orchestrator modules have been DELETED (the rollback
# window is closed) — these redirects, not any fallback page, are what serves these
# routes now. Kept at 302 so a future route change isn't hard-cached by browsers.
#
# Only the exact navigation routes are matched — never the shared assets still loaded
# by v2 under /macro/js, /credit/js, /legal/js, /premium.css, … (the desk DATA/shared
# modules remain) — so a wildcard must never be used here. Deep links into a desk are
# hash-based (/credit/#fund/x); the browser re-appends the fragment to the redirect
# target, and the v2 apps preserve hash sub-routing, so those links keep working.

/                    /v2/           302
/index.html          /v2/           302
/macro               /v2/macro/     302
/macro/              /v2/macro/     302
/macro/index.html    /v2/macro/     302
/credit              /v2/credit/    302
/credit/             /v2/credit/    302
/credit/index.html   /v2/credit/    302
/legal               /v2/legal/     302
/legal/              /v2/legal/     302
/legal/index.html    /v2/legal/     302
/menu                /v2/menu/      302
/menu/               /v2/menu/      302
/menu/index.html     /v2/menu/      302
